  "content": {
    "title": "Where to Watch the 2026 Oscars Online for Free Without Cable",
    "text": "If you purchase an independently reviewed product or service through a link on our website, Rolling Stone may receive an affiliate commission.The 98th Annual Academy Awards will take place this Sunday, March 15, 2026, at the Dolby Theatre in Los Angeles, California. Considered one of the biggest nights in Hollywood, this year’s ceremony will begin at 7:00 p.m. ET, with pre-event coverage starting at 6:30 p.m. ET.More from Rolling StoneIf you want to watch the major event online but don’t have a traditional cable subscription, we’ve outlined some of the best ways to stream the 2026 Oscars below.At a Glance: Where to Watch the 2026 Oscars Online for FreeChannel: ABCDate, time: Sunday, March 15, 2026 at 7 p.m. EST (pre-coverage starts at 6:30 p.m. EST) get directv trial This year’s broadcast will feature Conan O’Brien returning as host as millions of viewers tune in to see the Academy “recognize excellence in cinematic achievements.” Some of the nominees for Best Actor in a Major Motion Picture include Sinners‘ lead Michael B. Jordan and Timothée Chalamet, with viewers tuning in to see whether the Marty Supreme’s star’s recent comments about ballet and opera affected the votes. The Best Actress category, meantime, features nominees like Emma Stone and Rose Byrne.One of the most highly anticipated awards of the night is Best Picture, with films like F1, Hamnet, and One Battle After Another all vying for the coveted 24-karat gold statuette. And just how much of a lock is KPop Demon Hunters in the Animated Film and Original Song categories? Guess you’ll have to watch to find out.How to Watch the 2026 Oscars Online Without CableSince 1929, the Academy Awards have been a celebrated tradition that brings together the best of the film industry. Whether you’re watching from the comfort of your couch or hosting a viewing party with friends, there are several ways to stream the 2026 Oscars online without cable, and even for free.Don’t miss a moment of the event everyone will be talking, tweeting, and meme-ing about the next day. Read our guide below to learn how you can tune in live.Watch the Oscars With DirecTVEDITOR'S CHOICEWatch the Oscars With DirecTV get free trial ➤ $39.99/month➤ Five-day free trial➤ Up to 185+ channelsDirecTV is a solid way to catch the 2026 Oscars, thanks to its broad channel lineup that includes ABC in most markets. The MyNews pack starts at $39.99 per month and features major channels like ABC, NBC, CNN, and other leading news networks. Even better, every DirecTV plan begins with a five-day free trial.Watch the Oscars With FuboTOP PICKWatch the Oscars With Fubo get free trial ➤ $55.99/month➤ Five-day free trial➤ Up to 300+ channelsFubo is one of our favorite streaming platforms for live TV, and it’s a great option for watching the 2026 Oscars on ABC. New subscribers can start with a free trial, and after that the first month is $45.99, followed by a monthly price of $55.99.Watch the Oscars With Hulu + Live TV OFFICIAL STREAMERWatch the Oscars With Hulu + Live TV get free trial ➤ $89.99/month➤ Three-day free trial➤ 95+ channelsHulu + Live TV is one of the most complete streaming bundles available, making it an easy way to watch the 2026 Oscars live on ABC. Subscribers get access to Hulu, Disney+, ESPN+, and a full lineup of live channels. The ad-supported plan starts at $89.99 per month after a three-day free trial and includes 95+ channels. Hulu is the official streaming home of the 98th Academy Awards.Watch the Oscars With Sling ALSO CONSIDERWatch the Oscars With Sling get sling ➤ $45.99/month➤ Short-term passes available➤ Up to 46 channelsSling is another streaming option for tuning in to the 2026 Oscars, offering access to ABC through its Select, Blue, and Blue + Orange packages. It’s one of the more budget-friendly ways to stream live TV, with plans starting at $19.99 per month. There is no free trial.What Time Do the Oscars Start on Sunday?The 2026 Oscars ceremony begins at 7:00 p.m. ET, with pre-awards show coverage starting at 6:30 p.m. ET.How Can I Watch the Oscars for Free?You can watch the 2026 Oscars online for free by starting a free trial with DirecTV. Sign up below to begin streaming with no commitment. get directv trial What Movies Are Nominated for the Oscars This Year?The nominees this year for Best Picture are F1, Frankenstein, Train Dreams, One Battle After Another, Hamet, Bugonia, Sentimental Value, Marty Supreme, The Secret Agent and Sinners.The Best Original Song category once again features Diane Warren, who earned her 17th nomination. Warren, who was nominated for “Dear Me” from her documentary, Diane Warren: Relentless, has yet to win an Oscar, and she faces stiff competition from KPop Demon Hunters’ “Golden.”In a departure from previous award shows, the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences announced this year that only two of the Best Original Song nominees would get a “live performance focus:” those songs are “I Lied to You” from Sinners and “Golden” from KPop Demon Hunters. The three songs left out of the live telecast are Warren’s “Dear Me;” “Train Dreams” from Train Dreams, with music by Nick Cave and Bryce Dessner; and “Sweet Dreams of Joy” from Viva Verdi!, with music and lyrics by Nicholas Pike.Best of Rolling StoneSign up for RollingStone's Newsletter. For the latest news, follow us on Facebook, Twitter, and Instagram.",
